\title{The finite sum on a sign torus}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The cellular sign torus in \ref{fdip-00SM} has #{4} vertices
and #{8} labeled positive links. At mass #{5},
\ref{fdip-00U7} makes every matter determinant positive.
Fixing the links of a spanning tree leaves #{5} signs.
Which finite determinant calculation evaluates their sum,
and how does the matter weight change a loop average?}
